    <!-- First run -->
    <string name="firstrun_welcome_title">Welcome!</string>
    <string name="firstrun_welcome_text">QLauncher is a launcher for Android TV. It puts your apps, channels and favourite content on one customisable home screen, with a rotating wallpaper behind it.</string>
    <string name="firstrun_features_title">Your new superpowers</string>
    <string name="firstrun_features_text">Launch an app or an HDMI input at boot, manage display profiles, lock apps with parental control, show calibration patterns, detect idle time, and customise every part of the home screen. Some features depend on your device.</string>
    <string name="firstrun_a11y_title">Let\'s get accessible</string>
    <string name="firstrun_a11y_text">Many features need QLauncher\'s accessibility service: replacing the stock launcher, actions at boot, remote button gestures, idle detection and parental control. You can turn it on now or later from the settings.</string>
    <string name="firstrun_a11y_open">Open accessibility settings</string>
    <string name="firstrun_permissions_title">If I may…</string>
    <string name="firstrun_permissions_text">Next, QLauncher asks for permission to read TV listings (for channels and Watch Next) and for notification access (for the notification icon and Now Playing). Both are optional.</string>
    <!-- Before Android 8 there are no channels, so only notification access is asked for. -->
    <string name="firstrun_permissions_text_no_channels">Next, QLauncher asks for notification access (for the notification icon and Now Playing). It is optional.</string>
    <string name="firstrun_notifications_dialog">Allow notification access?</string>
    <string name="firstrun_notifications_text">Notification access lets QLauncher show a notification count, a notifications panel and what is playing. Yes opens the Special Permissions page where you grant it.</string>
    <string name="firstrun_reports_title">Send anonymous crash and error reports?</string>
    <string name="firstrun_reports_text">If QLauncher crashes or hits an error, it can send a report with the app version and device model so the bug can be fixed. Nothing that identifies you or what you watch is sent. You can change this later in General.</string>
    <string name="firstrun_launcher_title">Make QLauncher your home screen</string>
    <string name="firstrun_launcher_text">Many TV devices do not let you change the default launcher. If yours does, choose QLauncher there. Otherwise turn on the accessibility service with “Override current launcher”, and QLauncher will come back whenever the stock launcher opens.</string>
    <string name="firstrun_launcher_open">Change default launcher</string>
    <string name="firstrun_start_title">Time to start!</string>
    <string name="firstrun_start_text">Everything can be changed later from the settings. Press the settings button at the top right, or the key sequence ↑→↓←↑→↓←.</string>
